Example of a simple V-R-circuit in LTSPICE-syntax; This line is always the first line and names the 
* the circuit
* all following lines need a asterisk as first sign in order to be recognized as a comment
* inlinecomments are with  " ;" in front 


* First sign of a subcircuitcall always is a x od. X
* Call to the subcircuit "vri_slack"
Xv   v1r  v1i  vri_slack  params: vr=100 vi=0  ; subckt Aufruf with parameters
* v1r = inputnode real      v1i = inputnode imag   
* Call to the subcircuit "z_r"  
Xzr  v1r  v1i  v2r  v2i  z_r params: r=20  ; subckt Aufruf with parameters
* v1r = inputnode real      v1i = inputnode imag     v2r = outputnode real     v2i = ouputnode imag 

.subckt  vri_slack v1r   v1i  params: vr=100 vi=0
* First sign of a voltagesource always is a V od. v
V1r  v1r    0    {vr}  ; real part of voltage  v1r = outputnode+      0 = outputnode-  = Ground
V1i  v1i    0     {vi}  ; imag part of voltage  v1i = outputnode+     0 = outoputnode-  = Ground
.ends

.subckt z_r v1r  v1i  v2r  v2i  params: r=10  ; subckt-Definition with parameters
*G-Device voltagecontrolled currentsource I = f (V)  
g1r    v1r  0   value =  {1/r*v(v1r) }     ; voltagecontrolled currentsource ( eqn 1 ) 
* i1r = 1/r * v1r
g1i    v1i   0   value =  {1/r*v(v1i) }     ; voltagecontrolled currentsource ( eqn 2 )
* i1i = 1/r * v1i
.ends ; end of the subcircuits

.op  ;  ( operating point analysis )

* convergence parameters for the simulator 
.options reltol = 0.001  
* relative errortolerance for current and voltage between two subsequent iterations
.options abstol = 0.001 ; absolute. current errortolerance in A
.options vntol = 0.001 ; absolute voltage errortolerance in V 

.end ; End of circuit
